  "script": {
    "segments": [
      {
        "narration": "A face appeared in a woman's kitchen floor overnight. The 23rd of August, 1971. Belmez de la Moraleda, in Jaen, southern Spain.",
        "visual_query": "andalusian village white houses",
        "visual_fallback": "whitewashed village"
      },
      {
        "narration": "Maria Gomez Camara called her family in. They destroyed the image. A second face formed. This time the mayor ordered it preserved for study.",
        "visual_query": "old spanish tiled floor",
        "visual_fallback": "tiled floor"
      },
      {
        "narration": "By Easter 1972 hundreds of people were queuing at the house. Over thirty years more faces came and went. Nobody ever caught one in the act of appearing.",
        "visual_query": "rural spanish village street",
        "visual_fallback": "village street"
      },
      {
        "narration": "Then the laboratory answered it. Analysis of the floor turned up zinc, lead and chromium \u2014 the chemical signature of paint pigments.",
        "visual_query": "laboratory chemical analysis samples",
        "visual_fallback": "laboratory bench"
      },
      {
        "narration": "Infrared photography finished the job: pigment added over the original marks, with the bristle strokes of a paintbrush still visible inside them.",
        "visual_query": "infrared photography dark room",
        "visual_fallback": "dark room"
      }
    ],
